{% extends "layout.peb" %}
{% block content %}
<p class="notice">Zero allocation during lookup says nothing about objects already retained. Both benchmark query modes retain payloads; a streaming application need not retain this pool.</p>
<section><h2>Reachable query-pool graphs</h2>
<p>{{ method }}. Fresh input retains character arrays; reused, prehashed queries retain Strings and byte arrays. Both include the outer reference array. Measurements exclude membership structures, the harness, and transient per-operation String construction.</p>
{% set headers = ["Stored keys", "Query mode", "True hits", "Query payloads", "Reachable pool MiB", "Objects"] %}
{% include "table.peb" %}
<p><a href="query-pool.json">Raw measurements, JVM layout, and scope</a>. Add this JSON to the <code>queryPools</code> array in a review manifest to include it in a combined review.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
